From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm: TF_GLM_OVN_REPLY_PREFILL, the finished reply prefilled between turns

ai-engine 4c877aac0 grafted onto the pin stack (after 0007's any-row states).
GLM opts in to the server's background prompt-only pass at load: the pass
yields to waiting work (reply.gate) and runs capped chunks (_ROWS, default
256, on the 32-row grid; _QUIET_MS 10, refused off-grid or past a minute).
Leader.chunkOf carries the cap (capEnd); the warm pass loops it through the
pin's marks plumbing with the knob off leaving prefillFn's whole-prompt path
untouched. warmQuiet/warm_alone reach the lane host through the pin's
startup-phase serve. cuda_kda_chunk (the KDA_CHUNKED knob module, default
off) rides along: reply prefill's row validation reads its sub_rows. The
stepped prompt pass moved to cuda_lanes_step.zig (the 600-line rule) with the
lanes helpers it needs exposed pub. Core fix from the source commit kept:
warm_alone makes the quiet check end on any admitted job (a pass could run
inside a live request's step fill). GPU check glm-reply-prefill-check;
16 mutants killed at the source.

Gates on pin+0001..0008: check-native-cuda-host green, test-lane-api-host
green, whole-tree fmt green, lean base-vs-head 0 new.
